practiceProblems.description:
We can use the  'match'  statement to select one of many code blocks to be executed. 

The Syntax is as follows

    match expression {
        x => {
          // code 
        },
        y => {
          // code 
        },
        _ => {
           // code 
        },
    }

- The match expression is evaluated once, and the value of the expression is compared with the patterns of each arm. If there is a match, the associated block of code is executed.
- In Rust, each arm implicitly includes a break, meaning it will exit the match after the code for any matched arm is done. This stops the execution of more code and pattern testing inside the match.
- The "_" pattern specifies some code to run if there is no match.

Write a program which does the following
- Take input from the user with value between $1$ and $7$ 
- Compute and output to the console the day associated with that number.

